WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.934
-Looking good, bud.
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.234
-Thanks, man.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.234
-Thank you for being here.
-I'm a little offended.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.234
I just realized --

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.100
Like, I have a stylist lady.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.701
And she gives me suits --
no big deal -- to put on.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.968
It's stretchy.
-Oh. That's kind of fun.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.133
-It's a stretchy fabric.
-Is it fun?

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.601
-Uh, no. I'm offended by it.
-You are?

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.601
-She knows that I was gonna
overindulge at Thanksgiving,

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:24.667
and so --

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.834
-So she did that on purpose.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.434
-By the way,
how'd you like the parade?

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.467
You're in the parade this year.
-Yeah, it was so fun.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.667
I didn't -- Yeah, I was in
the Macy's Day Parade.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:39.501
I had no idea that it was
as big of a thing as it was.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.934
-Oh, it's a giant deal.
-It was huge.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.100
When they asked me,
they were like,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.234
"You want to be in
the Macy's Day Parade?"

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.901
I'm like, "What am I?
A beauty queen?

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.234
No, I don't want to be
in a parade."

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.801
I was with my dad
when they asked me,

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:51.534
and he's like, "You're
definitely not a beauty queen."

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.934
-Thanks, Dad.
-He's here, actually, today.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:57.300
He was like -- Not here for me.
He's here for Seinfeld.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.767
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:02.701
He's like, "Bring out Bruce!
Enough of you."

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.300
But, yeah, it's a huge deal.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.334
50 million people
watch the parade.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.300
-Yeah, it's a giant deal.
-It's a giant thing.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.334
Like, "Workaholics,"
which was my show,

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:13.234
I think, on our biggest episode,

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.334
like 3 1/2 million people
watched that.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.067
So this might be the
biggest thing I've ever done.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.267
-Yeah.
-The parade.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.901
I'm peaking on the float, baby.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.901
-Where are you from?
And where is your dad from?

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.033
-Omaha, Nebraska.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.834
My family's from Nebraska,
Midwest, yeah.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.100
-And how do they celebrate
Thanksgiving in the city?

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.033
Is that fun for them
or they don't like it?

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.234
-Well, it's weird being in
New York,

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:36.567
because, normally,
we're in the Midwest.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.934
But we have, like,

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:43.067
a whole big Thanksgiving dinner
planned at a steak house.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:46.534
And that was a mistake,
'cause, immediately,

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:49.434
my father was like,
"Oh, you're telling me

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:53.100
New York City cooks better
steaks than Omaha, Nebraska?"

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.834
-You're like,
"Alright, calm down, Dad."

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.067
-They're gonna be fine.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.634
This is one of the
biggest cities in the world.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:58.734
They can handle a steak.

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.133
He's like,
"I'll be the judge of that."

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.133
-Yeah. Oh, my gosh.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.968
Hey, I know you're doing
a lot of things.

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.467
I want to talk about
"Bumper in Berlin."

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:10.534
But you just finished a film
with Adam Sandler,

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:11.767
who is a good friend
of our show.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.267
We love Adam Sandler.
-Me too.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.734
-What a great guy.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.200
-The best.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.901
-I did this movie.
It's called "The Out-Laws."

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:21.801
It'll come out in --
sometime next year on Netflix.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.534
And he produced it,
I starred in it,

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:24.901
and we produced it together.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:27.734
And he's just an all-time great.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.968
-Did you ever do your
impression of him to him?

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.567
-No, because my impression is,
like, offensive.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.033
-It is?
-Yeah.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.801
It's not a good im--
I'm not a good impression--

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.300
You're a good impressionist.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.467
My impression is just,
like, the noises he makes.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.501
You know, that...
[ Speaks gibberish ]

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.033
No words.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.267
-Yeah, you don't want to do that
in front of him.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:50.667
-Unh-unh.
-Yeah. Alright.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.334
-[ Speaks gibberish ]

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.133
I'm gonna need another one.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.267
-Yeah, yeah.
-So...

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.968
-So you didn't do that.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.767
-But where did you meet Adam?

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.367
-I met him like years ago.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.234
The first time I met him,
I was like 19 or 20,

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.467
and I was working the door at

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:07.234
the Hollywood Improv
comedy club.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.567
And he came with
a group of friends,

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.467
and they were gonna go to
this cigar lounge next door.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.968
And I think I was, like,
staring at him just too --

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:18.167
just wide-eyed, just like,
"Ga-ga-ga-ga-ga."

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.701
So he's like, "Don't murder me."
-Yeah.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.133
-"Do you want to come
smoke a cigar with us?"

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.567
So I freaked out.
I was like, "Of course I'll go."

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.567
And then I awkwardly started --
I asked him.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.934
I was like,
"Did you remember that?"

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.634
He's like, "No."
And why would he?

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:36.400
Because I was just
some strange kid who was like...

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.567
[ Coughs ]

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:42.501
...who's never smoked a cigar in
his life, just choking it down.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:43.534
"Play it cool.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.133
You might be in a
'Grown Ups' movie."

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:46.834
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.634
-[ Speaks gibberish ]

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:51.167
-Can we talk about
"Bumper in Berlin"?

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.701
-Please.
-Congrats.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:56.067
This focuses on your character,
Bumper, from "Pitch Perfect."

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.200
And I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.567
-Yeah.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:03.834
-I had heard that Loki
was an inspiration for this.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:05.501
-Yeah, from the Marvel movies.
No joke.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:06.667
-How?

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.567
-Elizabeth Banks
was the producer of

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.634
the "Pitch Perfect" movies,
and she was like,

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:12.868
"It's cool that
they made the villain

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.734
the spin-off TV show" for Loki.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.067
-Yeah.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:21.701
-And, so, I'm the villain of
the "Bumper" franchise.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:25.400
-But there are a few nods to
"Pitch Perfect" in this --

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.934
-Yeah, we drop a
couple Easter eggs on 'em.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.968
-One of them is the cup song.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.234
-Oh, yeah.
-Which is legendary.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:36.834
-It's a wildly famous song.
-It's the biggest thing ever.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.701
I mean, did you remember
how to do it?

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:39.801
-No, I had to watch, like,

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.968
a YouTube tutorial
to try to remember.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.100
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.567
But I nailed it
in the show, so...

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.467
-Yeah, you kind of did, yeah.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.968
-Do you impress family members?

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.434
Like, "Hey,
I'll do the cup thing."

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.834
-No, all of my family --
they will do it for me.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.167
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.901
And they're like, "I bet
you can't do it as well as me."

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.000
Like, my little cousins.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.200
And I'm like,
"I bet you're right.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.234
You're 14.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:04.501
This is all you have
in your life.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.367
I got a life, girl."

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:09.667
-You upped your game.
You did it with a beer stein.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:10.701
-I did, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.701
-So eat it, Anna Kendrick.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.133
-No. No, no.
That's not what I'm saying.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:16.300
-No, I'm coming for you, Anna!
-That's not what I'm saying.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.567
-I'm coming for you!

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:21.467
-What I'm saying is,
we always have a beer stein.

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:23.767
-Oh, no!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.067
-Could you do it?
Would you get nervous?

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.000
Could you do it?
You don't have to do it.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.601
-Yeah, no, I'll -- I'll do it.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:37.267
And there's no possible way
I'll mess it up at all.

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:40.334
-Wow! That was nice slow moving
of the gourds.

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.267
-Yeah. You got to start
with it upside down.

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:43.834
This is a pro tip.
-Oh.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.934
-Okay, so...
[ Laughs ]

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:48.234
-I'm so excited about this.
-Watch this.

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:50.200
There's no way
I'm gonna mess it up.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.033
♪ When I'm gone ♪

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.834
♪ When I'm gone ♪

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.834
♪ You're gonna miss me
when I'm gone ♪

00:05:57.834 --> 00:05:59.734
♪ You're gonna miss me
by my talk ♪

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:02.400
♪ You're gonna miss me
by my walk, oh ♪

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.868
♪ You're gonna miss me when I'm

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:07.234
gone ♪

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:14.834
-Oh! That is how you do it right
there, ladies and gentlemen!

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.133
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:18.601
Here is Adam DeVine in
"Bumper in Berlin."

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.000
Take a look at this.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.200
-What if we turn this little
concert into a little riff-off?!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.534
-[ German accent ] Of course
you're challenging me

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:29.834
to a riff-off.

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:32.934
You Americans -- you are
obsessed with your riff-offs.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.934
-Wiff-off?
-Yeah, a riff-off.

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:36.200
-It's a riff-off.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.434
-Wiff-off.
-Riff-off.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.000
-You said "Riff-off,"
I said, "Riff-off."

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.267
-Okay.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:43.901
-And I would love to be
a part of the riff-off,

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:46.200
but, unfortunately,
the a cappella by-laws

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.434
clearly state a quorum of
a cappella peers

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:51.567
must be present for a
riff-off to be legally binding.

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:53.167
So it's sad, yeah.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.734
-It's actually not sad. Nein.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.767
-Yeah! Nein.
-Nein.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.133
-Adam DeVine, everyone.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:02.200
All six episodes of
"Bumper in Berlin"

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.300
are streaming
right now on Peacock.

